# Long-running command estimates

If a shell command, build, test, Fastlane, screenshot, or similar step is **estimated to take more than 5 minutes**, tell the user **before starting it**.

Include:
- What you are about to run (in plain language)
- A time estimate (range is fine, e.g. 8–15 minutes)

Do not silently start long `utility/build_and_test.sh`, full iOS simulator test, or Fastlane screenshot runs.

Typical RA11y durations (adjust if the machine is busy):
- Core-only build/test: usually under 5 minutes
- Full `utility/build_and_test.sh` (Core + iOS): often 10–40+ minutes, longer on a cold DerivedData / busy host
- Full Fastlane screenshot matrix: often 15+ minutes
